    {
      "id": "b3",
      "function": "explanation",
      "scene_type": "gs_section",
      "spoken": "Why so long? The whole line is 1,318 kilometres, and according to the trade press more than 85 percent of it runs on bridges and viaducts. So for most of the journey, the train rides on piers. This one bridge alone is about an eighth of the whole line.",
